('f38d554c-1d48-5fa6-8893-159bbe9fdbf4', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', 'c4c09cba-9d0a-4033-abe7-0b8c56bb7ef4', 'a-level', '23.6', '9702 coursebook 23.6 · Capacitor networks', 7, 7, 'A 2.0 µF and a 3.0 µF capacitor are in parallel, and the pair is in series with a 5.0 µF capacitor. Calculate the combined capacitance, in µF.', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2.5', 'µF', false, NULL, false, ARRAY['2.5e-6']::text[], 'Parallel pair: 2.0 + 3.0 = 5.0 µF. In series with 5.0 µF: C = 5.0 × 5.0 ÷ 10 = 2.5 µF. Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: reduce the parallel pair first. A1: C = 2.5 µF.', 2, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 270 146" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg5ff211c8-t fg5ff211c8-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg5ff211c8-t">Capacitor network</title><desc id="fg5ff211c8-d">Between A and B: a 2.0 µF and a 3.0 µF capacitor in parallel, in series with a 5.0 µF capacitor.</desc><line x1="40" y1="50" x2="56" y2="50" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="120" y1="50" x2="136" y2="50" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="56" y1="50" x2="56" y2="104" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="120" y1="50" x2="120" y2="104" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="56" y1="50" x2="83" y2="50" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="93" y1="50" x2="120" y2="50" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="83" y1="38" x2="83" y2="62" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="9