('d9811544-fe70-5a40-be35-bb88ab300483', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', 'c4c09cba-9d0a-4033-abe7-0b8c56bb7ef4', 'a-level', '23.6', '9702 coursebook 23.6 · Capacitor networks', 16, 16, 'A capacitor network that is equivalent to 4.5 µF is placed across 10 V. How much charge, in µC, leaves the supply?', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '45 uC', 'µC', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Q = CV = 4.5 × 10⁻⁶ × 10 = 4.5 × 10⁻⁵ C. In µC: 4.5 × 10⁻⁵ × 10⁶ = 45. Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: Q = C_total V. A1: Q = 45 µC.', 2, NULL, NULL),
('59e68dd7-b0ad-559a-9d1d-49bbf8c7783e', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', 'c4c09cba-9d0a-4033-abe7-0b8c56bb7ef4', 'a-level', '23.6', '9702 coursebook 23.6 · Capacitor networks', 17, 17, 'Three identical capacitors, each of capacitance C, are connected with two in series and that pair in parallel with the third. What is the combined capacitance?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, '1.5C', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Series pair C/2, plus C in parallel: 1.5C. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: B (1.5C).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('62cbe013-3fb1-5014-b708-b5f4a4b95023', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', 'c4c09cba-9d0a-4033-abe7-0b8c56bb7ef4', 'a-level', '23.6', '9702 coursebook 23.6 · Capacitor networks', 18, 18, 'A 6.0 µF capacitor is in series with a parallel pair made of a 2.0 µF and a 4.0 µF capacitor. Calculate the combined capacitance, in µF.', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '3', 'µF', false, NULL, false, ARRAY['3e-6']::text[], 'Parallel pair: 2.0 + 4.0 = 6.0 µF. In series with 6.0 µF: C = 6.0 ÷ 2 = 3.0 µF. Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: parallel then series. A1: C = 3.0 µF.', 2, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 270 146" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg00cf8a0e-t fg00cf8a0e-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg00cf8a0e-t">Capacitor network</title><desc id="fg00cf8a0e-d">Between A and B: a 6.0 µF capacitor in series with a 2.0 µF and a 4.0 µF capacitor in parallel.</desc><line x1="40" y1="50" x2="67" y2="50" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="77" y1="50" x2="104" y2="50" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="67" y1="38" x2="67" y2="62" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="77" y1="38" x2="77" y2="62" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="72" y="26" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">6.0 µF</text><line x1="104" y1="50" x2="120" y2="50" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="184" y1="50" x2="200" y2="50" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="120" y1="50" x2="120" y2="104" style="strok