"/><text x="8" y="38" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">A</text><line x1="222" y1="50" x2="200" y2="50" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="222" cy="50" r="4" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="232" y="38" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">B</text></svg>', 'Between A and B: a 6.0 µF capacitor in series with a 2.0 µF and a 4.0 µF capacitor in parallel.'),
('fe034bb2-771a-50ae-b346-9482fed25ba6', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', 'c4c09cba-9d0a-4033-abe7-0b8c56bb7ef4', 'a-level', '23.6', '9702 coursebook 23.6 · Capacitor networks', 19, 19, 'In a network, two capacitors are connected between the same pair of junctions. What is the same for both?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The p.d. across them', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Components between the same two junctions are in parallel. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: C (The p.d. across them).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('bc0e26fb-ce57-5695-b32f-81df4ef9889c', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', 'c4c09cba-9d0a-4033-abe7-0b8c56bb7ef4', 'a-level', '23.6', '9702 coursebook 23.6 · Capacitor networks', 20, 20, 'What is the equivalent capacitance, in µF, of a 100 µF capacitor in series with the parallel combination of 22 µF and 47 µF?', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '40.83', 'µF', false, NULL, false, ARRAY['4.083e-5']::text[], 'Parallel pair: 22 + 47 = 69 µF. In series with 100 µF: C = 69 × 100 ÷ 169 = 40.8 µF. Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: parallel then series. A1: C = 40.8 µF.', 2, NULL, NULL),
('93edd175-fb53-5eda-9bd5-9a69ef921199', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', 'c4c09cba-9d0a-4033-abe7-0b8c56bb7ef4', 'a-level', '23.6', '9702 coursebook 23.6 · Capacitor networks', 21, 21, 'Four 8.0 µF capacitors are arranged as two series pairs, and the pairs are connected side by side. Find the total capacitance, in µF.', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '8', 'µF', false, NULL, false, ARRAY['8e-6']::text[], 'Each series pair is 4.0 µF; in parallel: 4.0 + 4.0 = 8.0 µF. Mark scheme (1 mark). A1: C = 8.0 µF.', 1, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 270 146" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgd0dfb68e-t fgd0dfb68e-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgd0dfb68e-t">Capacitor network</title><desc id="fgd0dfb68e-d">Between A and B: two series pairs of 8.0 µF capacitors connected in parallel.</desc><line x1="40" y1="50" x2="56" y2="50" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="184" y1="50" x2="200" y2="50" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="56" y1="50" x2="56" y2="104" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="184" y1="50" x2="184" y2="104" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="56" y1="50" x2="83" y2="50" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="93" y1="50" x2="120" y2="50" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="83" y1="38" x2="83" y2="62" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="93" y1="38" x2="93" y2="62" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="88" y="26" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">8.0 µF</text><line x1="120" y1="50" x2="147" y2="50" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="157" y1="50" x2="184" y2="50" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="147" y1="38" x2="147" y2="62" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="157" y1="38" x2="157" y2="62" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="152" y="26" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">8.0 µF</text><line x1="56" y1="104" x2="83" y2="104" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="93" y1="104" x2="120" y2="104" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="83" y1="92" x2="83" y2="116" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="93" y1="92" x2="93" y2="116" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="88" y="80" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">8.0 µF</text><line x1="120" y1="104" x2="147" y2="104" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="157" y1="104" x2="184" y2="104" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="147" y1="92" x2="147" y2="116" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="157" y1="92" x2="157" y2="116" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="152" y="80" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">8.0 µF</text><circle cx="56" cy="50" r="3.2" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><circle cx="184" cy="50" r="3.2" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><line x1="18" y1="50" x2="40" y2="50" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="18" cy="50" r="4" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="8" y="38" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">A</text><line x1="222" y1="50" x2="200" y2="50" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="222" cy="50" r="4" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="232" y="38" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">B</text></svg>', 'Between A and B: two series pairs of 8.0 µF capacitors connected in parallel.'),
('00ca7256-4a8c-566b-9b73-347f8237fd07', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', 'c4c09cba-9d0a-4033-abe7-0b8c56bb7ef4', 'a-level', '23.6', '9702 coursebook 23.6 · Capacitor networks', 22, 22, 'What is (capacitance of three identical capacitors in parallel) ÷ (capacitance of the same three in series)?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, '9', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Parallel 3C; series C/3; ratio 9. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: A (9).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('6402ee7d-db14-51b5-bbb9-9a0f65d41670', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', 'c4c09cba-9d0a-4033-abe7-0b8c56bb7ef4', 'a-level', '23.6', '9702 coursebook 23.6 · Capacitor networks', 23, 23, 'A network that behaves as 2.0 µF is charged by a 50 V supply. What energy does it store, in mJ?', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2.5 mJ', 'mJ', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'W = ½CV² = 0.5 × 2.0 × 10⁻⁶ × 50² = 2.5 × 10⁻³ J. In mJ: 2.5 × 10⁻³ × 1000 = 2.5. Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: W = ½CV². A1: W = 2.5 mJ.', 2, NULL, NULL),
('757e6f9c-3292-5f91-85a3-0922b5ec6998', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', 'c4c09cba-9d0a-4033-abe7-0b8c56bb7ef4', 'a-level', '23.6', '9702 coursebook 23.6 · Capacitor networks', 24, 24, 'A 2.0 µF and a 4.0 µF capacitor in parallel are connected in series with a 3.0 µF capacitor across 12 V. Calculate the p.d. across the 3.0 µF capacitor.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '8', 'V', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Parallel pair 6.0 µF; total C = 6.0 × 3.0 ÷ 9.0 = 2.0 µF. Q = 2.0 × 10⁻⁶ × 12 = 2.4 × 10⁻⁵ C. V₃ = 2.4 × 10⁻⁵ ÷ 3.0 × 10⁻⁶ = 8.0 V. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: total C. C1: Q = CV. C1: V = Q/C for the series capacitor.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 300 236" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgde05a8df-t fgde05a8df-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgde05a8df-t">Capacitor network</title><desc id="fgde05a8df-d">A 2.0 µF and a 4.0 µF capacitor in parallel, in series with a 3.0 µF capacitor, across 12 V.</desc><line x1="26" y1="48" x2="42" y2="48" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="150" y1="48" x2="166" y2="48" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="42" y1="48" x2="42" y2="102" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="150" y1="48" x2="150" y2="102" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="42" y1="48" x2="91" y2="48" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="101" y1="48" x2="150" y2="48" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="91" y1="36" x2="91" y2="60" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="101" y1="36" x2="101" y2="60" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="96" y="24" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">2.0 µF</text><line x1="42" y1="102" x2="91" y2="102" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="101" y1="102" x2="150" y2="102" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="91" y1="90" x2="91" y2="114" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="101" y1="90" x2="101" y2="114" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="96" y="78" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">4.0 µF</text><circle cx="42" cy="48" r="3.2" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><circle cx="150" cy="48" r="3.2" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><line x1="166" y1="48" x2="215" y2="48" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="225" y1="48" x2="274" y2="48" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="215" y1="36" x2="215" y2="60" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="225" y1="36" x2="225" y2="60" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="220" y="24" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">3.0 µF</text><line x1="26" y1="196" x2="145" y2="196" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="155" y1="196" x2="274" y2="196" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="145" y1="183" x2="145" y2="209" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="155" y1="189" x2="155" y2="203" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="150" y="220" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">12 V</text><line x1="26" y1="48" x2="26" y2="196" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="274" y1="48" x2="274" y2="196" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></svg>', 'A 2.0 µF and a 4.0 µF capacitor in parallel, in series with a 3.0 µF capacitor, across 12 V.'),
('e9162a7c-e132-5d10-b0e5-7f1808a7d697', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', 'c4c09cba-9d0a-4033-abe7-0b8c56bb7ef4', 'a-level', '23.6', '9702 coursebook 23.6 · Capacitor networks', 25, 25, 'In a network, a 2.0 µF and a 4.0 µF capacitor are in parallel, and the pair is in series with a 3.0 µF capacitor across 12 V. The p.d. across the 3.0 µF capacitor is 8.0 V. Calculate the charge on the 4.0 µF capacitor, in µC.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '16 uC', 'µC', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'p.d. across the parallel pair: 12 − 8.0 = 4.0 V. Q = 4.0 × 10⁻⁶ × 4.0 = 1.6 × 10⁻⁵ C. In µC: 1.6 × 10⁻⁵ × 10⁶ = 16. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: p.d.s add to 12 V. C1: Q = CV. A1: Q = 16 µC.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 300 236" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg00ab3105-t fg00ab3105-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg00ab3105-t">Capacitor network</title><desc id="fg00ab3105-d">A 2.0 µF and a 4.0 µF capacitor in parallel, in series with a 3.0 µF capacitor, across 12 V; the 3.0 µF capacitor has 8.0 V across it.</desc><line x1="26" y1="48" x2="42" y2="48" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="150" y1="48" x2="166" y2="48" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="42" y1="48" x2="42" y2="102" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="150" y1="48" x2="150" y2="102" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="42" y1="48" x2="91" y2="48" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="101" y1="48" x2="150" y2="48" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="91" 