ound;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="155" y1="196" x2="274" y2="196" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="145" y1="183" x2="145" y2="209" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="155" y1="189" x2="155" y2="203" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="150" y="220" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">12 V</text><line x1="26" y1="48" x2="26" y2="196" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="274" y1="48" x2="274" y2="196" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></svg>', 'A 2.0 µF and a 4.0 µF capacitor in parallel, in series with a 3.0 µF capacitor, across 12 V; the 3.0 µF capacitor has 8.0 V across it.'),
('503f1065-a052-5800-9821-47d4f69c11ef', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', 'c4c09cba-9d0a-4033-abe7-0b8c56bb7ef4', 'a-level', '23.6', '9702 coursebook 23.6 · Capacitor networks', 26, 26, 'A branch of a 6.0 µF capacitor in series with a 3.0 µF capacitor is connected in parallel with a 4.0 µF capacitor, across a 9.0 V supply. Calculate the charge on the 3.0 µF capacitor, in µC.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '18 uC', 'µC', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Each branch has 9.0 V across it. Series branch: C = 6.0 × 3.0 ÷ 9.0 = 2.0 µF, so Q = 2.0 × 10⁻⁶ × 9.0 = 1.8 × 10⁻⁵ C on each of its capacitors. In µC: 1.8 × 10⁻⁵ × 10⁶ = 18. Mark scheme (4 marks). B1: each branch has the full 9.0 V. C1: series branch C. C1: Q = CV. A1: Q = 18 µC.', 4, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 300 236" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgf9d8e11a-t fgf9d8e11a-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgf9d8e11a-t">Capacitor network</title><desc id="fgf9d8e11a-d">A 6.0 µF capacitor in series with a 3.0 µF capacitor, in parallel with a 4.0 µF capacitor, across a 9.0 V supply.</desc><line x1="26" y1="48" x2="42" y2="48" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="258" y1="48" x2="274" y2="48" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="42" y1="48" x2="42" y2="102" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="258" y1="48" x2="258" y2="102" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="42" y1="48" x2="91" y2="48" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="101" y1="48" x2="150" y2="48" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;st