oke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="155" y1="196" x2="274" y2="196" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="145" y1="183" x2="145" y2="209" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="155" y1="189" x2="155" y2="203" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="150" y="220" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">9.0 V</text><line x1="26" y1="48" x2="26" y2="196" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="274" y1="48" x2="274" y2="196" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></svg>', 'A 6.0 µF capacitor in series with a 3.0 µF capacitor, in parallel with a 4.0 µF capacitor, across a 9.0 V supply.'),
('93ebcffb-9322-5322-abf8-2f6421c20f0f', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', 'c4c09cba-9d0a-4033-abe7-0b8c56bb7ef4', 'a-level', '23.6', '9702 coursebook 23.6 · Capacitor networks', 27, 27, 'Two capacitors are in series. A third capacitor is then connected in parallel with one of them. What happens to the combined capacitance?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'It increases', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'The parallel pair has a larger capacitance, so the series combination increases. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: parallel pair larger. C1: series total larger. A1: D (It increases).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('e033f687-e358-5b12-b18f-3a6a91006c2f', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', 'c4c09cba-9d0a-4033-abe7-0b8c56bb7ef4', 'a-level', '23.6', '9702 coursebook 23.6 · Capacitor networks', 28, 28, 'An unknown capacitor X is in series with a 6.0 µF capacitor, and a 2.0 µF capacitor is connected in parallel with this series pair. The combined capacitance is 5.0 µF. Calculate X, in µF.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '6', 'µF', false, NULL, false, ARRAY['6e-6']::text[], 'The series pair must be 5.0 − 2.0 = 3.0 µF. 1/X = 1/3.0 − 1/6.0, so X = 1 ÷ (1/3.0 − 1/6.0) = 6.0 µF. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: series pair = 3.0 µF. C1: reciprocal rule rearranged. A1: X = 6.0 µF.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 270 146" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg1f7a6b83-t fg1f7a6b83-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg1f7a6b83-t">Capacitor network</title><desc id="fg1f7a6b83-d">Between A and B: an unknown capacitor X in series with a 6.0 µF capacitor, with a 2.0 µF capacitor in parallel with the pair; the combined capacitance is 5.0 µF.</desc><line x1="40" y1="50" x2="56" y2="50" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="184" y1="50" x2="200" y2="50" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="56" y1="50" x2="56" y2="104" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="184" y1="50" x2="184" y2="104" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="56" y1="50" x2="83" y2="50" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="93" y1="50" x2="120" y2="50" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><li