('a37f8d44-fb5f-5d3e-9a36-32496583999b', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', 'c4c09cba-9d0a-4033-abe7-0b8c56bb7ef4', 'a-level', '23.6', '9702 coursebook 23.6 · Capacitor networks', 30, 30, 'A 2.0 µF capacitor is in series with a parallel pair made of a 6.0 µF and a 4.0 µF capacitor. Which capacitor has the largest p.d. across it when the network is connected to a supply?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The 2.0 µF capacitor', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'The parallel pair is 10 µF; in series, the smaller 2.0 µF takes five times the p.d. of the pair. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: parallel pair 10 µF. C1: V ∝ 1/C in series. A1: B (The 2.0 µF capacitor).', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 270 146" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg80105bf2-t fg80105bf2-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg80105bf2-t">Capacitor network</title><desc id="fg80105bf2-d">Between A and B: a 2.0 µF capacitor in series with a 6.0 µF and a 4.0 µF capacitor in parallel.</desc><line x1="40" y1="50" x2="67" y2="50" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="77" y1="50" x2="104" y2="50" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="67" y1="38" x2="67" y2="62" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="77" y1="38" x2="77" y2="62" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="72" y="26" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">2.0 µF</text><line x1="104" y1="50" x2="120" y2="50" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="184" y1="50" x2="200" y2="50" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.