('ab8b54c0-d109-54a3-a2fb-141efb7289a0', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', '0c42a207-4bd1-5379-b11d-d983544be962', 'a-level', '23.7', '9702 coursebook 23.7 · Discharging a capacitor', 22, 22, 'A 100 µF capacitor discharges through a resistor. Its p.d. falls from 10 V to 5.0 V in 6.9 s. Calculate the resistance, in kΩ.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '99.55', 'kΩ', false, NULL, false, ARRAY['99546']::text[], 'Half-life: t½ = RC ln 2, so RC = 6.9 ÷ ln 2 = 9.95 s. R = 9.955 ÷ 100 × 10⁻⁶ = 9.95 × 10⁴ Ω. In kΩ: 9.955 × 10⁴ ÷ 1000 = 99.5. Mark scheme (4 marks). M1: t½ = RC ln 2. C1: RC. C1: R = RC/C. A1: R = 99.5 kΩ.', 4, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg020d20d0-t fg020d20d0-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg020d20d0-t">Discharge curve</title><desc id="fg020d20d0-d">Graph of p.d. against time for a 100 µF capacitor discharging from 10 V; the p.d. reaches 5.0 V at 6.9 s (dashed lines).</desc><line x1="39.8" y1="34" x2="39.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="162" y1="34" x2="162" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="284.2" y1="34" x2="284.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="39.8" y1="242" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="39.8" y1="195.6" x2="382" y2="195.6" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="39.8" y1="149.1" x2="382" y2="149.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin: