('d27245f7-cf6d-5d23-92fb-a3b94371b281', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', '0c42a207-4bd1-5379-b11d-d983544be962', 'a-level', '23.7', '9702 coursebook 23.7 · Discharging a capacitor', 25, 25, 'A 220 µF capacitor discharges through a 47 kΩ resistor. Calculate the percentage of the initial charge remaining after 10 s.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '38.02', '%', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'RC = 47 × 10³ × 220 × 10⁻⁶ = 10.3 s. Q/Q₀ = e^(−10/10.34) = 0.3802. Percentage: 0.3802 × 100 = 38.0 %. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: RC. C1: e^(−t/RC). A1: percentage = 38.0%.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('c9c6827e-5c05-5dab-b8c5-00e0d72f2314', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', '0c42a207-4bd1-5379-b11d-d983544be962', 'a-level', '23.7', '9702 coursebook 23.7 · Discharging a capacitor', 26, 26, 'What fraction of the initial stored energy remains in a discharging capacitor after one time constant?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'About 0.14', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'W ∝ V², so W/W₀ = (e⁻¹)² = e⁻² ≈ 0.135. 0.37 is the charge fraction. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: W ∝ V². C1: e⁻². A1: C (About 0.14).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('a75f4f78-4d69-5c99-b895-9d5785e13dc2', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', '0c42a207-4bd1-5379-b11d-d983544be962', 'a-level', '23.7', '9702 coursebook 23.7 · Discharging a capacitor', 27, 27, 'A capacitor discharges with a time constant of 3.0 s. Calculate the time taken for its stored energy to halve.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.04', 's', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'W ∝ V² ∝ e^(−2t/RC). Setting e^(−2t/RC) = ½ gives t = RC ln 2 ÷ 2 = 3.0 × ln 2 ÷ 2 = 1.04 s. Mark scheme (4 marks). M1: W ∝ e^(−2t/RC). C1: logs. C1: substitution. A1: t = 1.04 s.', 4, NULL, NULL),
('1c333440-daa2-5f24-91f9-02238cb81a37', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', '0c42a207-4bd1-5379-b11d-d983544be962', 'a-level', '23.7', '9702 coursebook 23.7 · Discharging a capacitor', 28, 28, 'A graph of ln(V/V) against t for a discharging capacitor has a gradient of −0.25 s⁻¹. The resistor is 20 kΩ. Calculate the capacitance, in µF.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '200', 'µF', false, NULL, false, ARRAY['2e-4']::text[], 'Gradient = −1/RC, so RC = 1 ÷ 0.25 = 4.0 s. C = 4.0 ÷ 20 × 10³ = 2.0 × 10⁻⁴ F. In µF: 2.0 × 10⁻⁴ × 10⁶ = 200. Mark scheme (3 marks). M1: gradient = −1/RC. C1: C = RC/R. A1: C = 200 µF.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgd8ae1913-t fgd8ae1913-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgd8ae1913-t">ln V against time</title><desc id="fgd8ae1913-d">Graph of ln(V/V) against time for a discharging capacitor: a straight line with a gradient of −0.25 s⁻¹.</desc><line x1="33" y1="34" x2="33" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="115.1" y1="34" x2="115.1" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="197.3" y1="34" x2="197.3" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="279.4" y1="34" x2="279.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="361.5" y1="34" x2="361.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="33" y1="242" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="33" y1="200.4" x2="382" y2="200.4" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="33" y1="158.8" x2="382" y2="158.8" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="33" y1="117.2" x2="382" y2="117.2" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="33" y1="75.6" x2="382" y2="75.6" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="33" y1="242" x2="388" y2="242" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="33" y1="242" x2="33" y2="28" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="392,242 385.7,245 385.7,239" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><polygon points="33,24 36,30.3 30.1,30.3" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><line x1="33" y1="242" x2="33" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="33" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="115.1" y1="242" x2="115.1" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="115.1" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">2</text><line x1="197.3" y1="242" x2="197.3" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="197.3" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">4</text><line x1="279.4" y1="242" x2="279.4" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="279.4" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">6</text><line x1="361.5" y1="242" x2="361.5" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="361.5" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">8</text><line x1="29" y1="242" x2="33" y2="242" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="26" y="242" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="29" y1="200.4" x2="33" y2="200.4" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="26" y="200.4" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0.5</text><line x1="29" y1="158.8" x2="33" y2="158.8" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="26" y="158.8" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">1.0</text><line x1="29" y1="117.2" x2="33" y2="117.2" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="26" y="117.2" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">1.5</text><line x1="29" y1="75.6" x2="33" y2="75.6" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="26" y="75.6" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">2.0</text><text x="207.5" y="274" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">t / s</text><text x="29" y="14" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">ln(V/V)</text><polyline points="33,59 361.5,225.4" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="207.3" y="134.2" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">gradient −0.25 s⁻¹</text></svg>', 'Graph of ln(V/V) against time for a discharging capacitor: a straight line with a gradient of −0.25 s⁻¹.'),
('5eaf572a-5bdd-5a8f-b58c-e4ebf2ebe1e2', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', '0c42a207-4bd1-5379-b11d-d983544be962', 'a-level', '23.7', '9702 coursebook 23.7 · Discharging a capacitor', 29, 29, 'Why does the discharge current of a capacitor decrease with time?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'As the charge falls, the p.d. across the capacitor falls, so the current V/R falls', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'I = V/R and V = Q/C, so the rate of loss of charge is proportional to the charge left. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: V falls with Q. C1: I = V/R. A1: A (As the charge falls, the p.d. across the capacitor falls, so the current V/R falls).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('1f81405b-b3f4-51cf-b9a5-7ed496d04f72', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', '0c42a207-4bd1-5379-b11d-d983544be962', 'a-level', '23.7', '9702 coursebook 23.7 · Discharging a capacitor', 30, 30, 'A capacitor initially holds 6.0 mC and discharges through a circuit with RC = 3.0 s. Calculate the initial discharge current, in mA.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2 mA', 'mA', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'I₀ = Q₀/RC = 6.0 × 10⁻³ ÷ 3.0 = 2.0 × 10⁻³ A. In mA: 2.0 × 10⁻³ × 1000 = 2.0. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: I₀ = V₀/R = Q₀/RC. C1: conversion. A1: I₀ = 2.0 mA.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('ea70fa51-fa73-53f4-8b3f-995cfdde2b19', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', '0c42a207-4bd1-5379-b11d-d983544be962', 'a-level', '23.7', '9702 coursebook 23.7 · Discharging a capacitor', 31, 31, 'How many time constants does it take for the p.d. across a discharging capacitor to fall to 1.0 % of its initial value?', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '4.605', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '0.010 = e^(−t/RC), so t/RC = ln 100 = 4.61. Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: V/V₀ = 0.010. M1: natural logs. C1: value. A1: t/RC = 4.61.', 4, NULL, NULL),
('56840262-aa52-551b-874e-a08ceb4a2696', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', '0c42a207-4bd1-5379-b11d-d983544be962', 'a-level', '23.7', '9702 coursebook 23.7 · Discharging a capacitor', 32, 32, 'Two identical capacitors discharge through identical resistors, one starting from 12 V and the other from 6.0 V. How do the times for their p.d.s to halve compare?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'They are the same', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'The half-life RC ln 2 does not depend on the starting value. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: t½ = RC ln 2. C1: independent of V₀. A1: D (They are the same).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('df897a0d-0225-5573-91c2-3db9f77caa24', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', '0c42a207-4bd1-5379-b11d-d983544be962', 'a-level', '23.7', '9702 coursebook 23.7 · Discharging a capacitor', 33, 33, 'A 0.22 F memory-backup capacitor discharges through a 47 kΩ load. Calculate the time constant, in hours.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2.872', 'hours', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'RC = 47 × 10³ × 0.22 = 1.03 × 10⁴ s. In hours: 1.034 × 10⁴ ÷ 3600 = 2.87. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: RC. C1: seconds to hours. A1: τ = 2.87 hours.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('09270358-f8f9-5eac-8125-fbf336d10aac', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', '0c42a207-4bd1-5379-b11d-d983544be962', 'a-level', '23.7', '9702 coursebook 23.7 · Discharging a capacitor', 34, 34, 'In a camera sensor, a 100 nF capacitor at 5.0 V is drained through 10 kΩ. What is its p.d. 2.0 ms later?', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.6767', 'V', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'RC = 10 × 10³ × 100 × 10⁻⁹ = 1.0 × 10⁻³ s. V = 5.0 × e^(−2.0) = 0.677 V. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: RC. C1: V = V₀e^(−t/RC). A1: V = 0.677 V.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('f847c43c-9e07-5b3c-8988-742fe335a734', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', '0c42a207-4bd1-5379-b11d-d983544be962', 'a-level', '23.7', '9702 coursebook 23.7 · Discharging a capacitor', 35, 35, 'How is the half-life t½ of a capacitor discharge related to the time constant RC?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 't½ = RC ln 2 ≈ 0.69RC', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Setting Q = Q₀/2 in Q = Q₀e^(−t/RC) gives t = RC ln 2. Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: Q = Q₀/2. C1: logs. C1: ln 2 ≈ 0.69. A1: B (t½ = RC ln 2 ≈ 0.69RC).', 4, NULL, NULL),
('4774cc73-9b6e-5386-97fe-14669654b3a4', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', '0c42a207-4bd1-5379-b11d-d983544be962', 'a-level', '23.7', '9702 coursebook 23.7 · Discharging a capacitor', 36, 36, 'A capacitor initially holding 5.0 mC discharges through a resistor. Calculate the charge that flows through the resistor during the first time constant, in mC.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '3.161 mC', 'mC', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Remaining: 5.0e⁻¹; flowed = 5.0 × (1 − e^(−1)) = 3.16 mC. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: Q = Q₀e⁻¹ remaining. C1: difference. A1: ΔQ = 3.16 mC.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('2ce967f4-a659-5b9b-b39e-8a6b9290240b', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', '0c42a207-4bd1-5379-b11d-d983544be962', 'a-level', '23.7', '9702 coursebook 23.7 · Discharging a capacitor', 37, 37, 'A 1000 µF capacitor charged to 20 V discharges completely through a resistor. Calculate the total energy dissipated in the resistor.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.2', 'J', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'All the stored energy is converted to heat: W = 0.5 × 1000 × 10⁻⁶ × 20² = 0.20 J. Mark scheme (4 marks). B1: all stored energy dissipated. C1: W = ½CV². C1: substitution. A1: W = 0.20 J.', 4, NULL, NULL),
('44718347-9cb9-599a-8713-ef1424fc82db', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', '0c42a207-4bd1-5379-b11d-d983544be962', 'a-level', '23.7', '9702 coursebook 23.7 · Discharging a capacitor', 38, 38, 'A high-resistance digital voltmeter (10 MΩ) is connected across a charged 1.0 µF capacitor. Why does its reading slowly fall?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The capacitor discharges through the voltmeter with a time constant of about 10 s', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'RC = 10 × 10⁶ × 1.0 × 10⁻⁶ = 10 s, so the reading decays noticeably within seconds. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: meter provides discharge path. C1: RC ≈ 10 s. A1: C (The capacitor discharges through the voltmeter with a time constant of about 10 s).', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 276.9 146" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg3154e1fc-t fg3154e1fc-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg3154e1fc-t">Voltmeter across a capacitor</title><desc id="fg3154e1fc-d">A charged 1.0 µF capacitor with a 10 MΩ digital voltmeter connected across it.</desc><line x1="40" y1="50" x2="56" y2="50" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="190.9" y1="50" x2="206.9" y2="50" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="56" y1="50" x2="56" y2="104" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="190.9" y1="50" x2="190.9" y2="104" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="56" y1="50" x2="118.4" y2="50" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="128.4" y1="50" x2="190.9" y2="50" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="118.4" y1="38" x2="118.4" y2="62" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="128.4" y1="38" x2="128.4" y2="62" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.6;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="123.4" y="26" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">1.0 µF</text><line x1="56" y1="104" x2="111.4" y2="104" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="135.4" y1="104" x2="190.9" y2="104" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="123.4" cy="104" r="12" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="123.4" y="104.5" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">V</text><text x="123.4" y="80" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">10 MΩ voltmeter</text><circle cx="56" cy="50" r="3.2" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><circle cx="190.9" cy="50" r="3.2" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><line x1="18" y1="50" x2="40" y2="50" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="18" cy="50" r="4" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="8" y="38" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">A</text><line x1="228.9" y1="50" x2="206.9" y2="50" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="228.9" cy="50" r="4" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="238.9" y="38" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">B</text></svg>', 'A charged 1.0 µF capacitor with a 10 MΩ digital voltmeter connected across it.'),
('5b89e8f5-0e87-5499-b36c-589964c081f1', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', '0c42a207-4bd1-5379-b11d-d983544be962', 'a-level', '23.7', '9702 coursebook 23.7 · Discharging a capacitor', 39, 39, 'A capacitor discharges through a 100 kΩ resistor. The p.d. is recorded: t/s = 0, 10, 20, 30, 40 and V/V = 12.0, 7.3, 4.4, 2.7, 1.6. (a) Explain why a graph of ln(V/V) against t should be a straight line. (b) Calculate the gradient using the first and last readings. (c) Calculate the time constant. (d) Calculate the capacitance, in µF. Give only the answer to (d).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '198.5', 'µF', false, NULL, false, ARRAY['1.985e-4']::text[], '(a) V = V₀e^(−t/RC), so ln V = ln V₀ − t/RC: linear in t. (b) Gradient = (ln 1.6 − ln 12.0) ÷ 40 = −0.0504 s⁻¹. (c) RC = −1 ÷ gradient = 40 ÷ (ln 12.0 − ln 1.6) = 19.9 s. (d) C = 19.85 ÷ 100 × 10³ = 1.99 × 10⁻⁴ F. In µF: 1.985 × 10⁻⁴ × 10⁶ = 199. Mark scheme (6 marks). B1: ln V linear in t. C1: gradient. M1: gradient = −1/RC. C1: RC. C1: C = RC/R. A1: C = 199 µF.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 438" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgda739c23-t fgda739c23-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgda739c23-t">Discharge readings</title><desc id="fgda739c23-d">Table and graph of p.d. against time for a capacitor discharging through 100 kΩ: t = 0, 10, 20, 30, 40 s give V = 12.0, 7.3, 4.4, 2.7, 1.6 V, an exponential decay.</desc><g transform="translate(0,0)"><rect x="142.7" y="8" width="114.6" height="168" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="142.7" y="8" width="114.6" height="28" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="170.6" y="22" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">t / s</text><text x="228" y="22" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">V / V</text><line x1="198.6" y1="8" x2="198.6" y2="176" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="142.7" y1="36" x2="257.3" y2="36" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="170.6" y="50" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><text x="228" y="50" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">12.0</text><line x1="142.7" y1="64" x2="257.3" y2="64" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="170.6" y="78" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">10</text><text x="228" y="78" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">7.3</text><line x1="142.7" y1="92" x2="257.3" y2="92" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="170.6" y="106" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">20</text><text x="228" y="106" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">4.4</text><line x1="142.7" y1="120" x2="257.3" y2="120" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="170.6" y="134" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">30</text><text x="228" y="134" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">2.7</text><line x1="142.7" y1="148" x2="257.3" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="170.6" y="162" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">40</text><text x="228" y="162" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">1.6</text></g><g transform="translate(0,188)"><line x1="29.4" y1="34" x2="29.4" y2="202" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="109.6" y1="34" x2="109.6" y2="202" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="189.7" y1="34" x2="189.7" y2="202" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="269.8" y1="34" x2="269.8" y2="202" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="349.9" y1="34" x2="349.9" y2="202" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="202" x2="382" y2="202" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="150.3" x2="382" y2="150.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="98.6" x2="382" y2="98.6" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="46.9" x2="382" y2="46.9" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="202" x2="388" y2="202" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="202" x2="29.4" y2="28" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="392,202 385.7,205 385.7,199" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><polygon points="29.4,24 32.4,30.3 26.5,30.3" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><line x1="29.4" y1="202" x2="29.4" y2="206" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="29.4" y="214" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="109.6" y1="202" x2="109.6" y2="206" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="109.6" y="214" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">10</text><line x1="189.7" y1="202" x2="189.7" y2="206" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="189.7" y="214" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">20</text><line x1="269.8" y1="202" x2="269.8" y2="206" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="269.8" y="214" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">30</text><line x1="349.9" y1="202" x2="349.9" y2="206" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="349.9" y="214" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">40</text><line x1="25.4" y1="202" x2="29.4" y2="202" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="202" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="25.4" y1="150.3" x2="29.4" y2="150.3" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="150.3" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">4</text><line x1="25.4" y1="98.6" x2="29.4" y2="98.6" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="98.6" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">8</text><line x1="25.4" y1="46.9" x2="29.4" y2="46.9" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="22.4" y="46.9" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">12</text><text x="205.7" y="234" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">t / s</text><text x="25.4" y="14" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">V / V</text><line x1="25.4" y1="42.9" x2="33.4" y2="50.9" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="25.4" y1="50.9" x2="33.4" y2="42.9" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="105.6" y1="103.7" x2="113.6" y2="111.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="105.6" y1="111.7" x2="113.6" y2="103.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="185.7" y1="141.1" x2="193.7" y2="149.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="185.7" y1="149.1" x2="193.7" y2="141.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="265.8" y1="163.1" x2="273.8" y2="171.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="265.8" y1="171.1" x2="273.8" y2="163.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="345.9" y1="177.3" x2="353.9" y2="185.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="345.9" y1="185.3" x2="353.9" y2="177.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></g></svg>', 'Table and graph of p.d. against time for a capacitor discharging through 100 kΩ: t = 0, 10, 20, 30, 40 s give V = 12.0, 7.3, 4.4, 2.7, 1.6 V, an exponential decay.'),
('6d425200-989b-5771-81cb-75417975c790', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', '0c42a207-4bd1-5379-b11d-d983544be962', 'a-level', '23.7', '9702 coursebook 23.7 · Discharging a capacitor', 40, 40, 'The p.d. across a 470 µF capacitor discharging through a resistor halves every 3.5 s. (a) Show that the half-life is RC ln 2. (b) Calculate the time constant. (c) Calculate the resistance, in kΩ. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '10.74', 'kΩ', false, NULL, false, ARRAY['10743']::text[], '(a) V₀/2 = V₀e^(−t/RC) gives t = RC ln 2. (b) RC = 3.5 ÷ ln 2 = 5.05 s. (c) R = 5.049 ÷ 470 × 10⁻⁶ = 1.07 × 10⁴ Ω. In kΩ: 1.074 × 10⁴ ÷ 1000 = 10.7. Mark scheme (5 marks). M1: half-life from exponential. C1: RC = t½/ln 2. C1: R = RC/C. C1: conversion to kΩ. A1: R = 10.7 kΩ.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgfb7a6561-t fgfb7a6561-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgfb7a6561-t">Halving every 3.5 s</title><desc id="fgfb7a6561-d">Graph of p.d. against time for a 470 µF capacitor: the p.d. falls from V₀ to V₀/2 at 3.5 s, V₀/4 at 7.0 s and V₀/8 at 10.5 s.</desc><line x1="42.2" y1="34" x2="42.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="127.1" y1="34" x2="127.1" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="212.1" y1="34" x2="212.1" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="297" y1="34" x2="297" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="34" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;st