.1 360.8,228.2 361.6,228.3 362.5,228.4 363.3,228.5 364.2,228.6 365,228.7 365.9,228.8 366.7,228.9 367.6,228.9 368.4,229 369.3,229.1 370.1,229.2 371,229.3 371.8,229.4 372.7,229.5 373.5,229.6 374.4,229.6 375.2,229.7 376.1,229.8 376.9,229.9 377.8,230 378.6,230.1 379.5,230.1 380.3,230.2 381.2,230.3 382,230.4" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></svg>', 'Graph of p.d. against time for a 470 µF capacitor: the p.d. falls from V₀ to V₀/2 at 3.5 s, V₀/4 at 7.0 s and V₀/8 at 10.5 s.'),
('b2a2af9d-e39b-5e9c-82b0-9107d4f65235', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', '0c42a207-4bd1-5379-b11d-d983544be962', 'a-level', '23.7', '9702 coursebook 23.7 · Discharging a capacitor', 41, 41, 'A defibrillator capacitor of 32 µF is charged to 5.0 kV and discharges through a patient''s chest, of resistance 50 Ω. (a) Calculate the time constant, in ms. (b) Calculate the initial current. (c) Calculate the energy delivered to the patient in the first 2.0 ms. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '367.2', 'J', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) RC = 50 × 32 × 10⁻⁶ = 1.6 × 10⁻³ s, which is 1.6 ms. (b) I₀ = 5.0 × 10³ ÷ 50 = 100 A. (c) W₀ = 0.5 × 32 × 10⁻⁶ × (5.0 × 10³)² = 400 J. W ∝ V², so the energy left is W₀e^(−2t/RC) and the energy delivered = 400 × (1 − e^(−2 × 2.0/1.6)) = 367 J. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: RC. C1: I₀ = V₀/R. C1: W₀ = ½CV². M1: W ∝ e^(−2t/RC). C1: energy delivered. A1: W = 367 J.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('f4fcb6e1-2721-57d8-bf68-043330d409b4', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', '0c42a207-4bd1-5379-b11d-d983544be962', 'a-level', '23.7', '9702 coursebook 23.7 · Discharging a capacitor', 42, 42, '(a) Starting from Q = Q₀e^(−t/RC), show that ln Q = ln Q₀ − t/RC. (b) A 220 µF capacitor discharges through a 15 kΩ resistor. Calculate the time taken for it to lose 75 % of its charge. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '4.575', 's', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) Taking natural logs: ln Q = ln Q₀ + ln e^(−t/RC) = ln Q₀ − t/RC. (b) RC = 15 × 10³ × 220 × 10⁻⁶ = 3.3 s. 25 % remains: 0.25 = e^(−t/RC), so t = 3.3 × ln 4 = 4.57 s. Mark scheme (5 marks). B1: logs taken correctly. C1: RC. M1: 25 % remains. C1: t = RC ln 4. A1: t = 4.57 s.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('bd02f10c-0458-5141-a5de-67b5c21f491f', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', '0c42a207-4bd1-5379-b11d-d983544be962', 'a-level', '23.7', '9702 coursebook 23.7 · Discharging a capacitor', 43, 43, 'A timer circuit switches a light off when the p.d. across a discharging 1000 µF capacitor falls from 9.0 V to 3.0 V. The delay must be 60 s. (a) Show that the delay is RC ln 3. (b) Calculate the resistance needed, in kΩ. (c) Suggest why the actual delay might differ from 60 s. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '54.61', 'kΩ', false, NULL, false, ARRAY['54614']::text[], '(a) V/V₀ = e^(−t/RC) with V₀/V = 3, so t = RC ln 3. (b) RC = 60 ÷ ln 3 = 54.6 s. R = 54.61 ÷ 1000 × 10⁻⁶ = 5.46 × 10⁴ Ω. In kΩ: 5.461 × 10⁴ ÷ 1000 = 54.6. (c) Capacitors have a wide tolerance (often ±20 %) and can leak, and the switching p.d. may vary. Mark scheme (5 marks). M1: V/V₀ = 1/3. C1: RC. C1: R in kΩ. B1: tolerance or leakage. A1: R = 54.6 kΩ.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg4ae40d04-t fg4ae40d04-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg4ae40d04-t">Timer discharge</title><desc id="fg4ae40d04-d">Graph of p.d. against time for the 1000 µF timer capacitor discharging from 9.0 V; the light switches off when the p.d. reaches 3.0 V, after the 60 s delay.</desc><line x1="39.8" y1="34" x2="39.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="96.8" y1="34" x2="96.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="153.8" y1="34" x2="153.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="210.9" y1="34" x2="210.9" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-wi