('64f762d7-f1be-5d9e-bda0-63e70effbe8a', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', '0c42a207-4bd1-5379-b11d-d983544be962', 'a-level', '23.7', '9702 coursebook 23.7 · Discharging a capacitor', 44, 44, 'A 100 µF capacitor charged to 10 V discharges through a 20 kΩ resistor for 2.0 s. The resistor is then switched to 5.0 kΩ and the discharge continues. (a) Calculate the p.d. after the first 2.0 s. (b) Calculate the new time constant. (c) Calculate the p.d. 1.0 s after the switch. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.4979', 'V', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) RC₁ = 20 × 10³ × 100 × 10⁻⁶ = 2.0 s; V = 10 × e^(−1) = 3.68 V. (b) RC₂ = 5.0 × 10³ × 100 × 10⁻⁶ = 0.50 s. (c) V = 3.679 × e^(−1.0/0.50) = 0.498 V. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: first RC. C1: V after 2.0 s. C1: second RC. M1: new decay starts from the p.d. at the switch. C1: final V. A1: V = 0.498 V.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg887d8867-t fg887d8867-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg887d8867-t">Two-stage discharge</title><desc id="fg887d8867-d">Graph of p.d. against time: the 100 µF capacitor discharges from 10 V through 20 kΩ (RC = 2.0 s) until 2.0 s, then much faster through 5.0 kΩ (RC = 0.5 s).</desc><line x1="39.8" y1="34" x2="39.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="108.2" y1="34" x2="108.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="176.7" y1="34" x2="176.7" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="245.1" y1="34" x2="245.1" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><