('a55f618f-03a7-5244-a44c-f0d7053349e9', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', '0c42a207-4bd1-5379-b11d-d983544be962', 'a-level', '23.7', '9702 coursebook 23.7 · Discharging a capacitor', 45, 45, 'Because its dielectric is not a perfect insulator, an isolated 4.7 µF capacitor loses half its p.d. in 2.0 hours. (a) Calculate the time constant. (b) Calculate the leakage resistance, in GΩ. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2.21', 'GΩ', false, NULL, false, ARRAY['2.21e9']::text[], '(a) RC = t½ ÷ ln 2 = 7200 ÷ ln 2 = 1.04 × 10⁴ s. (b) R = 1.039 × 10⁴ ÷ 4.7 × 10⁻⁶ = 2.21 × 10⁹ Ω. In GΩ: 2.210 × 10⁹ ÷ 10⁹ = 2.21. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: hours to seconds. M1: RC = t½/ln 2. C1: R = RC/C. C1: conversion to GΩ. A1: R = 2.21 GΩ.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('3ac007c7-4cab-5c94-9513-6746888d6de8', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', '0c42a207-4bd1-5379-b11d-d983544be962', 'a-level', '23.7', '9702 coursebook 23.7 · Discharging a capacitor', 46, 46, 'A capacitor initially charged to 9.0 V discharges through a resistor. The current is 0.50 mA at the start and 0.18 mA after 20 s. (a) Calculate the time constant. (b) Calculate the initial charge, using Q₀ = I₀RC. (c) Calculate the capacitance, in µF. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1088', 'µF', false, NULL, false, ARRAY['0.001088']::text[], '(a) I = I₀e^(−t/RC), so RC = t ÷ ln(I₀/I) = 20 ÷ ln(0.50/0.18) = 19.6 s. (b) Q₀ = 0.50 × 10⁻³ × 19.58 = 0.00979 C. (c) C = Q₀/V₀ = 0.009788 ÷ 9.0 = 0.00109 F. In µF: 0.001088 × 10⁶ = 1090. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: logs of current ratio. C1: RC. M1: Q₀ = I₀RC. C1: C = Q₀/V₀. C1: conversion to µF. A1: C = 1090 µF.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg1177bde9-t fg1177bde9-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg1177bde9-t">Discharge current</title><desc id="fg1177bde9-d">Graph of discharge current against time: 0.50 mA at the start, falling exponentially to 0.18 mA after 20 s.</desc><line x1="33" y1="34" x2="33" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="91.2" y1="34" x2="91.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="149.4" y1="34" x2="149.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="207.5" y1="34" x2="207.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="265.7" y1="34" x2="265.7" y2="242" style="