('1afeed5a-9835-5832-ab4e-95a291509b3e', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', '0c42a207-4bd1-5379-b11d-d983544be962', 'a-level', '23.7', '9702 coursebook 23.7 · Discharging a capacitor', 47, 47, 'A 470 µF capacitor charged to 12 V discharges through a 1.0 kΩ resistor. (a) Calculate the initial power dissipated in the resistor. (b) Show that the power falls as e^(−2t/RC). (c) Calculate the power after one time constant, in mW. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '19.49 mW', 'mW', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) P₀ = V₀²/R = 12² ÷ 1000 = 0.144 W. (b) P = V²/R and V ∝ e^(−t/RC), so P ∝ e^(−2t/RC). (c) P = 0.144 × e^(−2) = 0.0195 W. In mW: 0.01949 × 1000 = 19.5. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: P = V²/R. B1: P ∝ e^(−2t/RC). C1: e⁻² factor. C1: conversion to mW. A1: P = 19.5 mW.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg66a35f97-t fg66a35f97-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg66a35f97-t">Discharge curve</title><desc id="fg66a35f97-d">Graph of p.d. against time for a 470 µF capacitor discharging from 12 V through 1.0 kΩ (time constant 0.47 s).</desc><line x1="29.4" y1="34" x2="29.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="117.6" y1="34" x2="117.6" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="205.7" y1="34" x2="205.7" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="293.9" y1="34" x2="293.9" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="34" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;st