('e77dd16f-18d1-53bb-8c08-58655d798892', '34322ed1-8148-406d-97ee-947a4eca6b7f', '0c42a207-4bd1-5379-b11d-d983544be962', 'a-level', '23.7', '9702 coursebook 23.7 · Discharging a capacitor', 50, 50, 'In a pacemaker, a 2.0 µF capacitor charged to 5.0 V discharges through heart tissue of resistance 500 Ω. The pulse ends when the p.d. has fallen to 1.0 V. (a) Calculate the time constant. (b) Calculate the duration of the pulse, in ms. (c) Calculate the charge delivered during the pulse, in µC. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.609 ms', 'ms', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) RC = 500 × 2.0 × 10⁻⁶ = 1.0 × 10⁻³ s. (b) V₀/V = 5, so t = RC ln 5 = 1.0 × 10⁻³ × ln 5 = 0.00161 s. In ms: 0.001609 × 1000 = 1.61. (c) ΔQ = C × ΔV = 2.0 × 10⁻⁶ × (5.0 − 1.0) = 8.0 × 10⁻⁶ C, which is 8.0 µC. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: RC. M1: V/V₀ = 1/5. C1: t = RC ln 5. C1: conversion to ms. C1: ΔQ = CΔV. A1: t = 1.61 ms.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgfd19d528-t fgfd19d528-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgfd19d528-t">Pacemaker pulse</title><desc id="fgfd19d528-d">Graph of p.d. against time in ms for a 2.0 µF capacitor discharging from 5.0 V through 500 Ω (time constant 1.0 ms); the pulse ends when the p.d. reaches 1.0 V (dashed line).</desc><line x1="24" y1="34" x2="24" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="113.5" y1="34" x2="113.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="203" y1="34" x2="203" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="292.5" y1="34" x2="292.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill: